$4x^{7} + \sqrt[5]{x} - \frac{1}{\sqrt[7]{x^{13}}}$."} {:db/id 17592186233644 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8f7dc381-ff4a-5ab2-9c80-1b180b43d77b" :question/math-academy-id "q-2252" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $2{x}^{2}-x+\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\begin{aligned}\int (2{x}^{2}-x+\frac{1}{2})\,\text{d}x & =2\int {x}^{2}\,\text{d}x-\int x\,\text{d}x+\int \frac{1}{2}\,\text{d}x \\  & =2\left(\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\right)-\left(\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\right)+\left(\frac{x}{2}\right)+C \\  & =\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3}-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\frac{x}{2}+C.\end{aligned}\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186234106 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b6c1d13e-58bd-57d8-918b-0a1bebf09fb1" :question/math-academy-id "q-49173" :question/problem "$\int {(1+5{x}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\int {(1+5{x}^{2})}^{2}\,\text{d}x & =\int (1+10{x}^{2}+25{x}^{4})\,\text{d}x \\  & =25\int {x}^{4}\,\text{d}x+10\int {x}^{2}\,\text{d}x+\int 1\,\text{d}x \\  & =25\left(\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\right)+10\left(\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\right)+(x)+C \\  & =5{x}^{5}+\frac{10{x}^{3}}{3}+x+C.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186250124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4d74b89-75a1-56f3-b6b6-828088510585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{3}{\sqrt[3]{x}}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id 17592186249171} {:answer/id #uuid "de570091-257b-5378-a03a-2502b905ef6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{3}{\sqrt[3]{x}}+\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id 17592186249396} {:answer/id #uuid "e77f388d-8a73-59ce-8f66-bc9a394fa477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{3}{\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id 17592186249466} {:answer/id #uuid "f18e54e2-bbf7-5c09-a529-02ac0e448d1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+4{x}^{4}+\frac{x}{2}+C" :db/id 17592186249545} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f381b4-0b8f-5cfb-8192-5f7af284e5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\sqrt[3]{x}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\frac{x}{4}+C" :db/id 17592186249595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4d74b89-75a1-56f3-b6b6-828088510585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\frac{3}{\sqrt[3]{x}}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\frac{1}{x}+C" :db/id 17592186249171} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb1b4399-41fb-5b60-b839-8a80147e6a2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186249996}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e132caee-594d-5f81-b6a1-2e2a44a2d5f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-113848" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of 
$\frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\int (\frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\,\text{d}x & =\int {x}^{-4/3}\,\text{d}x+\int {x}^{3}\,\text{d}x-\int {x}^{-2}\,\text{d}x \\  & =\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{(-\frac{4}{3}+1)}+\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{(3+1)}-\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}+C \\  & =\frac{{x}^{-1/3}}{\left(-\frac{1}{3}\right)}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\frac{{x}^{-1}}{(-1)}+C \\  & =-\frac{3}{\sqrt[3]{x}}+\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\frac{1}{x}+C.\end{aligned}
$$"} {:db/id 17592186567046 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37dd99bc-3607-581f-978c-a71b67914c2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}-2{x}^{2}-\frac{2}{3{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id 17592186566477} {:answer/id #uuid "9126a86d-bcfd-5fec-9571-5503eba42ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{5\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}}{9}-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\frac{2}{3{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id 17592186566648} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d265ad-a1a6-58b0-b6d6-e96a59278366" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{9}{5\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}}-\frac{2}{x}-\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id 17592186566688} {:answer/id #uuid "dafdca6c-9141-5612-9f79-f5c98e819afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{4}{\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}}-\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}-\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}+C" :db/id 17592186566803} {:answer/id #uuid "f64dcd14-9eac-5db3-bba6-758aa5bc23bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{5\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}}{4}-\frac{1}{2x}-\frac{2}{3{x}^{6}}+C" :db/id 17592186566857}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9126a86d-bcfd-5fec-9571-5503eba42ee5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\frac{5\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}}{9}-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\frac{2}{3{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id 17592186566648} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1056adf-eded-5bde-8128-44705a2baad4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186566981}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "676d4494-4f46-573f-a890-2a8daa607201" :question/math-academy-id "q-113850" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of 
$\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}-x+\frac{2}{{x}^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get

$$
\begin{aligned}\int (\sqrt[5]{{x}^{4}}-x+\frac{2}{{x}^{4}})\,\text{d}x & =\int {x}^{4/5}\,\text{d}x-\int x\,\text{d}x+2\int {x}^{-4}\,\text{d}x \\  & =\frac{{x}^{4/5+1}}{(\frac{4}{5}+1)}-\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{(1+1)}+2\cdot \frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{(-4+1)}+C \\  & =\frac{{x}^{9/5}}{\left(\frac{9}{5}\right)}-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2\cdot \frac{{x}^{-3}}{(-3)}+C \\  & =\frac{5\sqrt[5]{{x}^{9}}}{9}-\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\frac{2}{3{x}^{3}}+C.\end{aligned}
$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Sums of Power Functions"}
